WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:12.267
Bottom line: use one ALM path; ship a managed artifact, set target config, move data apart, and do DLP, test, license and approval checks before final go-live.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.567
Treat the suite as one platform for apps, flows, sites, agents and Dataverse data.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:24.067
Put lifecycle, security, test and release choices in one clear decision frame.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.067
Build change in an unmanaged solution, with source control as the source of truth.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:35.467
Export a managed solution as the build artifact that test and production receive.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.033
Keep configuration and business records on separate tracks.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:47.600
Set connections, references and variables per target, then migrate table rows, because solutions carry no data.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:53.767
Automate with pipelines, or use Azure DevOps or GitHub when the route needs it.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:59.700
Before final production, check DLP policy, tests, analytics, approvals and licenses.
